{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce a specific offence banning protests outside people's homes",
        "additional_details": "We think the country is experiencing increasingly violent and intimidating protests outside the homes of refugees, immigrants, MPs, local authority workers, and other groups, including incidents where houses have been attacked.\r\n\r\nEven without direct violence the protests are terrifying for the targeted people and their neighbours. We feel that allowing such protests fails to protect people\u2019s rights under Article 8 of the Human Rights Act.",
        "background": "Protests that target homes or take place on residential streets should be made illegal to prevent harm to communities, families and individuals. People have a legal and moral right to live in their homes or other accommodation with privacy, security and dignity, and this should be protected.  \r\n",
